                "asynchronous_ai_overview": false,
                "markdown": "![Hebrew letter Tav Stock Vector Image &amp; Art - Alamy](https://api.dataforseo.com/cdn/i/10110526-2762-0139-0000-2aa65438bb87:4)\nTav (ת) is the 22nd and final letter of the Hebrew alphabet , carrying the numerical value of 400.[[1]](https://www.chabad.org/library/article_cdo/aid/137287/jewish/Tav.htm)\n\n### Key Facts and Symbolism\n\n- **Pronunciation:** Usually makes a \"T\" sound (as in \"table\"), though in some traditional or Ashkenazi contexts it can be pronounced like an \"S\".[[1]](https://learnhebrewforchristians.com/hebrew-alphabet/tav)\n- **Ancient Form:** In early pictographic and Phoenician scripts, Tav looked like a cross or an \"X\" mark (+), representing a sign, seal, or signature. It is the historical ancestor of the Greek letter Tau and the Latin letter T.[[1]](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taw)[[2]](https://learnhebrewforchristians.com/hebrew-alphabet/tav)\n- **Meaning:** It translates to \"mark,\" \"sign,\" or \"signature\", and is deeply tied to the concept of *emet* (truth), which spans the alphabet from Aleph to Tav.[[1]](https://www.chabad.org/library/article_cdo/aid/137287/jewish/Tav.htm)[[2]](https://learnhebrewforchristians.com/hebrew-alphabet/tav)\n- **Spiritual Significance:** In Jewish tradition, it represents completion, perfection, and the seal of creation. In the Hebrew Bible (Ezekiel 9:4), it is described as a mark placed on the foreheads of the righteous.[[1]](https://learnhebrewforchristians.com/hebrew-alphabet/tav)[[2]](https://gabrielelevy.com/pages/the-letter-tav)[[3]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mp1OSr7v8ZM&t=6)\n\nWould you like to learn about **words starting with Tav** or explore its **gematria and mystical meanings** further?",
